		<preamble GUID="_3cd63a73-9985-4435-b8e9-f96e4afb433f" eId="preamble"><?DMS-Component componentId="c9ce16f4-7922-4ab0-a31d-e521dd135d4d" seriesId="9807cfb6-1658-40af-a9fb-80131283ef54" versionNumber="1"?>
			
			<formula GUID="_91c7b54b-c882-4393-97ab-52fc6afb7387" eId="preamble__enactingWords" name="enactingText">
				<p>The Secretary of State makes the following <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType" /> in exercise of the powers conferred by sections 1(1) and 18(2) of the Safety of Sports Grounds Act 1975<authorialNote GUID="_b3514a99-b7e0-4cf7-a371-40a113eefc5c" class="footnote" eId="fnote_1" marker="1">
						<p>1975 c. 52; section 1(1) was amended by Schedule 2 to the Fire Safety and Safety of Places of Sport Act 1987 (c. 27).</p>
					</authorialNote>.</p>
				<p>The Secretary of State is of the opinion that the condition in section 1(1) of that Act is satisfied<authorialNote GUID="_4014385e-a176-4e5e-a741-6b148a4aa17f" class="footnote" eId="fnote_2" marker="2">
						<p>By section 1(1) of the Safety of Sports Grounds Act 1975, the Secretary of State may by order designate as a sports ground requiring a safety certificate under that Act any sports ground which, in the Secretary of State’s opinion, has accommodation for more than 10,000 spectators. The Safety of Sports Grounds (Accommodation of Spectators) Order 1996 (S.I. 1996/499) substituted the number 5,000 for the number of spectators specified in section 1(1) of that Act in respect of sports grounds in England and Wales at which association football matches are played and which are occupied by a football club which is a member of the Football League Limited or the Football Association Premier League Limited.</p>
					</authorialNote> and has, in accordance with section 18(4) of that Act, consulted with such persons and bodies of persons as appear requisite to the Secretary of State.</p>
			</formula>
		</preamble>
		<body><?DMS-Component componentId="eae4b2b3-65fa-435c-846b-8248a7258328" seriesId="346a21b8-10d0-4a1e-8563-eb11a4447b70" versionNumber="1"?>
			
			<article GUID="_765fa45e-df34-46e6-9ccc-f3f71bde2267" class="prov1" eId="art_1"><?DMS-Component componentId="c0ed9b49-b59c-48ec-8d49-342526ea2800" seriesId="6c9fa4bd-4447-4a36-9f0e-810c31a7aba1" versionNumber="1"?>
				
				<heading GUID="_f81a8473-7f59-4378-b532-b907d82693e0" eId="art_1__hdg">Citation, commencement and extent</heading>
				<num>1.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_b3c14054-34a6-4f4d-8745-ee20f47de080" class="prov2" eId="art_1__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>This Order may be cited as the Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) (Amendment) (England) Order 2023 and comes into force on 30th March 2023.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_e5bf4f20-38ac-498e-8c67-a84591c281be" class="prov2" eId="art_1__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>This Order extends to England and Wales.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</article>
			<article GUID="_02a74ecc-a078-4368-bcf5-e2174367ee70" class="prov1" eId="art_2"><?DMS-Component componentId="004a7345-5720-4bb0-b8fc-7d67e1df3ee1" seriesId="4b131a07-65a0-417a-a840-23ae24aaf7d8" versionNumber="1"?>
				
				<heading GUID="_c3bc4252-20cb-4618-9340-a74fb9f144aa" eId="art_2__hdg">Amendment to the Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) Order 2015</heading>
				<num>2.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_6792cf8c-ef7f-4624-b8ca-d9f801885a3a" class="prov2" eId="art_2__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>The Safety of Sports Grounds (Designation) Order 2015<authorialNote GUID="_3acefa14-2aa1-48a8-9d40-48799bd4e09d" class="footnote" eId="fnote_3" marker="3">
								<p>S.I. 2015/661, to which there are amendments not relevant to this Order.</p>
							</authorialNote> is amended as follows.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_56060e20-a74a-44d9-b6a5-1416a069fe73" class="prov2" eId="art_2__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>
							<mod>In Schedule 1 (sports grounds designated under article 2(1)), after the entry for AJ Bell Stadium, occupied by Sale Rugby Union Football Club, and Salford Red Devils Rugby Football League Club, insert—<quotedStructure GUID="_18258ee5-1e81-4b0e-9a6a-e0e13fe9adf9" eId="art_2__para_2__qstr" endQuote="”" startQuote="“" ukl:context="body" ukl:docName="uksi" ukl:indent="indent0">
									<content>
										<tblock GUID="_590df5d1-7d79-420e-9d14-83177e742476" class="table" eId="art_2__para_2__qstr__tbl__oc_1">
											<foreign>
												<table xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:akn="http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0" class="middleVertical tableleft width100" cols="2">
													<tbody class="left">
														<tr akn:GUID="_3661e560-63a2-4395-ad83-0f9b06ed79a5" akn:eId="art_2__para_2__qstr__tbl__oc_1__row__oc_1">
															<td akn:GUID="_c7bafe9d-f596-42fd-9ec8-352da5ad6985" akn:eId="art_2__para_2__qstr__tbl__oc_1__row__oc_1__col_1">
																<p xmlns="http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0">StoneX Stadium, Greenlands Lane, London, NW4 1RL</p>
															</td>
															<td akn:GUID="_09796037-2c6e-4a7e-b7e0-50af53655fbb" akn:eId="art_2__para_2__qstr__tbl__oc_1__row__oc_1__col_2">
																<p xmlns="http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0">Saracens Rugby Club</p>
															</td>
														</tr>
													</tbody>
												</table>
											</foreign>
										</tblock>
									</content>
								</quotedStructure><inline name="AppendText">.</inline></mod>
						</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</article>
			<hcontainer GUID="_348fa429-80cd-48ed-a928-ed693da87a3c" eId="sigs" name="signatures"><?DMS-Component componentId="696d7fa7-1e49-4f27-bf50-8c8c77295589" seriesId="11e0a380-4eed-451d-ba8c-d85c944a4d3b" versionNumber="0"?>
				
				<hcontainer GUID="_5eb7f18e-35d5-41cf-a8b8-b1c844c6a156" eId="sigs__sigBlk" name="signatureBlock">
					<content>
						<block GUID="_1844b81c-defc-4fe7-b8c5-f077921dbdf0" eId="sigs__sigBlk__sig" name="signature">Stuart Andrew</block>
						<block GUID="_a30358e9-d4d5-4033-a32e-6dddf955b7e7" eId="sigs__sigBlk__role" name="role">Parliamentary Under Secretary of State</block>
						<block name="date"><date date="2023-03-06">6th March 2023</date></block>
						<block GUID="_f739cd22-c36e-4f86-847f-d943aa02debd" eId="sigs__sigBlk__org" name="organization">Department for Culture, Media and Sport</block>
					</content>
